      "side": 1,
      "message": "Test cases modify the LDAP ServiceAddresses to two server URIs via Config LDAP URLs, but lack a [Teardown] to restore the original single-server configuration. After they run, the BMC\u0027s LDAP ServiceAddresses is left as a two-address list ([${LDAP_SERVER_URI}, \u003cbad\u003e] or [\u003cbad\u003e, ${LDAP_SERVER_URI}]). Since these cases could run before other cases that assume the single ${LDAP_SERVER_URI} (e.g. Verify LDAP Login With Correct LDAP URL) — especially with randomized execution order — this leftover state can cause inconsistent results and pollute the DUT. Please add a [Teardown] to restore the LDAP URL, following the existing pattern in this file, e.g.:\n\n[Teardown]  Run Keywords  Restore LDAP URL  AND\n...  FFDC On Test Case Fail",
